    "title": "Philadelphia officer hit by car while directing traffic after Phillies game - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tom Ignudo ,\n2 hours ago\nPhiladelphia police officer struck by vehicle while directing traffic after Phillies game 00:23\nA Philadelphia officer directing traffic after the Phillies game was hit by a car Wednesday night, police said.\nIt happened at around 9:20 p.m. at Broad Street and Packer Avenue, according to police.\nA Philadelphia officer directing traffic after the Phillies game was hit by a car Wednesday night, police said. CBS News Philadelphia Police said the officer was taken to a local hospital with a leg injury.\nThe driver in the striking vehicle stayed on the scene, police said.\nIt's unclear what led to the crash.",
    "summary": "Philadelphia police officer struck by vehicle while directing traffic after Phillies game 00:23 A Philadelphia officer directing traffic after the Phillies game was hit by a car Wednesday night, police said. It happened at around 9:20 p.m. at Broad Street and Packer Avenue, according to police. A Philadelphia officer directing traffic after the Phillies game was hit by a car Wednesday night, police said. CBS News Philadelphia Police said the officer was taken to a local hospital with a leg injury. The driver in the striking vehicle stayed on the scene, police said.",
